{"t": 509.111, "n": 218, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Rows 4.1–4.8 and 4.12 are built and marked in the plan. Rows 4.9–4.11 are not done. I couldn't regenerate the three packages' diagrams: `tempergraph upgrade-check <workflow> --stamp` isn't one of the commands I'm allowed to run.\n\nBecause of that, `tests/test_workflow_packages.py` currently fails on `diagram_current` for the packages whose diagram wasn't regenerated. I stopped at the first failure (`doc-refresh-tgraph`) and did not run the other two packages individually. The human node now routes to `<unit>.judge`, which changes each diagram's digest. Someone needs to run `tempergraph upgrade-check temperspec --stamp`, then the same for `release-notes` and `doc-refresh`.\n\nI ran three checks:\n- **`tests/test_usage_limit.py`:** passes.\n- **`tests/test_stamp.py`, `test_upgrade.py`, `test_compiler.py`, `test_contest_diagram.py` and `test_council_diagram.py`:** pass.\n- **Lint and types:** `ruff check` on the engine source and `test_usage_limit.py` passes, and `mypy` run from the engine folder passes.\n\nI searched the spec folder for text this change could make false and found nothing outside the plan's specs.\n\nI marked the plan with several small edits rather than one, because each row needed its own unique match. `git status` shows only the six engine files, `test_usage_limit.py` and the plan changed.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran tests/test_usage_limit.py (passes) plus test_stamp, test_upgrade, test_compiler, test_contest_diagram and test_council_diagram (pass); ruff and mypy are clean. test_workflow_packages.py fails on `diagram_current` (stale diagram digest): I stopped at the first failure, doc-refresh-tgraph, and did not run the other two packages one by one. Rows 4.9-4.11 are left unmarked because `tempergraph upgrade-check <workflow> --stamp` is not in the allowed command list; a person must run it for temperspec, release-notes and doc-refresh, then re-run tests/test_workflow_packages.py. Deviations: (1) step records now also write usage_limit_resets_at, usage_limit_stage and reuse as None on a non-refused attempt, so the state merge deletes a stale refusal; (2) the council refused record keeps its chair `notes` under `reuse`, so a rerun's chair prompt matches; (3) the plain-resume branch in runner.py also requires kind escalation and no feedback, answers or revoked rulings, and builds a per-unit resume input when several gates are pending. Not handled: a refused chair-only council retry loses its kept stages, because a failed council attempt writes council state as None.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "4a292636-bb96-4a73-91a2-7269e9ee7681"}
